1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,204
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:06,094
Momo coils a long wire round a new iron nail, and joins

3
00:00:06,114 --> 00:00:07,804
its two ends to a battery.

4
00:00:08,084 --> 00:00:10,444
The nail attracts some steel paper clips.

5
00:00:10,714 --> 00:00:12,584
Then she takes the battery away.

6
00:00:12,854 --> 00:00:14,444
What happens to the clips?

7
00:00:14,503 --> 00:00:16,103
One, they stay on the nail.

8
00:00:17,353 --> 00:00:18,723
Two, they drop off.

9
00:00:20,202 --> 00:00:21,712
Hold on to your answer!

10
00:00:23,784 --> 00:00:26,454
We are building a mini crane for Recycling Week.

11
00:00:26,524 --> 00:00:29,024
It must lift the steel scrap into the lorry.

12
00:00:29,146 --> 00:00:31,426
My bar magnet picks up the steel caps.

13
00:00:31,446 --> 00:00:33,086
But it never lets them go!

14
00:00:33,287 --> 00:00:35,997
A little millipede is hiding in this video.

15
00:00:36,247 --> 00:00:37,487
Can you spot it?

16
00:00:37,611 --> 00:00:39,851
Look low, near the plants and the floor!

17
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,360
You against the Buddies!

18
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:43,480
Lock in first with your fingers.

19
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:45,580
One finger for every point.

20
00:00:46,161 --> 00:00:47,331
Today you'll learn:

21
00:00:47,528 --> 00:00:48,978
The electrical method.

22
00:00:49,184 --> 00:00:50,184
On and off.

23
00:00:50,386 --> 00:00:51,446
Stay safe.

24
00:00:51,949 --> 00:00:52,889
Are you ready?

25
00:00:53,329 --> 00:00:54,099
Three!

26
00:00:54,479 --> 00:00:55,139
Two!

27
00:00:55,509 --> 00:00:56,159
One!

28
00:00:56,579 --> 00:00:57,299
Go!

29
00:00:58,688 --> 00:00:59,578
Round one!

30
00:00:59,888 --> 00:01:01,758
Momo takes the battery away.

31
00:01:02,018 --> 00:01:03,608
What happens to the clips?

32
00:01:03,898 --> 00:01:05,198
Show me your fingers!

33
00:01:08,670 --> 00:01:09,650
Locked in!

34
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:10,388
One!

35
00:01:10,518 --> 00:01:12,398
Pip's stroked nail stayed a magnet.

36
00:01:12,558 --> 00:01:14,928
So Momo's nail will stay a magnet too!

37
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:15,870
Two.

38
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:18,100
I watched the crane across the road.

39
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:21,180
Its big disc drops the scrap all by itself.

40
00:01:21,232 --> 00:01:21,832
Two.

41
00:01:22,052 --> 00:01:24,932
The clips jumped up when I joined the battery, so they will

42
00:01:24,952 --> 00:01:26,292
drop without it.

43
00:01:26,568 --> 00:01:27,858
Be the iron nail!

44
00:01:28,188 --> 00:01:29,168
Shrink down.

45
00:01:29,448 --> 00:01:30,378
Quietly.

46
00:01:32,664 --> 00:01:35,664
You are a new iron nail, lying on the table.

47
00:01:36,444 --> 00:01:40,744
A long wire wraps round you, round and round, in neat turns.

48
00:01:41,269 --> 00:01:44,159
The wire's two ends are joined to the battery.

49
00:01:44,939 --> 00:01:46,719
Now you feel a pull at your tip!

50
00:01:47,489 --> 00:01:50,139
The steel clips jump up, and cling to you.

51
00:01:50,654 --> 00:01:52,654
Then the battery is taken away.

52
00:01:53,424 --> 00:01:54,684
The pull is gone.

53
00:01:55,454 --> 00:01:58,474
The clips let go, and drop back into the tray!

54
00:02:00,139 --> 00:02:02,579
The answer is two: the clips drop off!

55
00:02:02,839 --> 00:02:04,429
Did you show two fingers?

56
00:02:04,659 --> 00:02:06,060
Put one finger up!

57
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:09,280
The electrical method is a way to make a magnet that uses

58
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:14,010
electricity from a battery, such as my long wire and my battery!

59
00:02:14,738 --> 00:02:18,338
Is Momo's nail still a little magnet, like Pip's stroked nail?

60
00:02:18,989 --> 00:02:20,139
Look closer.

61
00:02:20,719 --> 00:02:22,229
The battery is away.

62
00:02:22,819 --> 00:02:24,929
Dip the nail into the steel clips.

63
00:02:25,499 --> 00:02:27,101
The clips stay in the tray.

64
00:02:27,121 --> 00:02:30,011
Join the battery again, and the clips jump up.

65
00:02:30,571 --> 00:02:32,504
Take it away, and they drop.

66
00:02:32,524 --> 00:02:36,652
Without electricity, the nail loses most of its magnetism.

67
00:02:36,672 --> 00:02:39,512
The crane across the road works the same way.

68
00:02:40,092 --> 00:02:43,122
Switched on, its big round disc lifts the scrap.

69
00:02:43,692 --> 00:02:45,295
Switched off, it lets go!

70
00:02:45,315 --> 00:02:49,465
An electromagnet is a magnet that is made with electricity, such as

71
00:02:49,485 --> 00:02:51,075
Momo's coiled nail!

72
00:02:54,372 --> 00:02:55,662
Say it with me!

73
00:02:56,376 --> 00:03:00,016
A magnet made by this method is called an electromagnet.

74
00:03:02,638 --> 00:03:04,458
One battery makes a magnet.

75
00:03:04,528 --> 00:03:07,118
So the wall socket will make a super magnet!

76
00:03:07,178 --> 00:03:09,008
Let's join our wire to it!

77
00:03:09,138 --> 00:03:10,698
Something is not right.

78
00:03:10,968 --> 00:03:13,148
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

79
00:03:13,428 --> 00:03:14,388
Hold on!

80
00:03:19,801 --> 00:03:20,931
Arms crossed?

81
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:22,411
One finger up!

82
00:03:22,463 --> 00:03:23,523
Stop, Momo!

83
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:26,663
Electricity from the wall socket is far too strong.

84
00:03:26,903 --> 00:03:28,413
It can hurt you very badly.

85
00:03:28,573 --> 00:03:30,043
We only use batteries!

86
00:03:30,172 --> 00:03:33,536
Wall sockets give us the main electrical supply.

87
00:03:33,556 --> 00:03:37,496
Do not connect the electromagnet to the battery for too long as

88
00:03:37,516 --> 00:03:39,336
the objects may become hot.

89
00:03:39,586 --> 00:03:42,746
Do not touch the exposed wires with your bare hands.

90
00:03:43,026 --> 00:03:47,226
Do not connect the electromagnet to the main electrical supply.

91
00:03:47,954 --> 00:03:51,104
I think the battery is a magnet, and the wire just joins

92
00:03:51,124 --> 00:03:52,144
it to the nail.

93
00:03:52,796 --> 00:03:53,946
Look closer.

94
00:03:54,526 --> 00:03:56,956
The battery alone attracts no clips.

95
00:03:57,526 --> 00:04:00,354
The iron nail alone attracts no clips.

96
00:04:00,374 --> 00:04:03,724
Coil the wire round the nail, and join just one end to

97
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:04,614
the battery.

98
00:04:05,204 --> 00:04:06,264
Still nothing.

99
00:04:06,284 --> 00:04:07,904
Now join both ends.

100
00:04:08,484 --> 00:04:12,374
Electricity flows from the battery, round the nail, and back.

101
00:04:12,944 --> 00:04:14,682
The nail becomes a magnet!

102
00:04:14,702 --> 00:04:18,322
Coil means wind round and round, in neat turns, such as the

103
00:04:18,342 --> 00:04:20,452
long wire round Momo's nail!

104
00:04:23,752 --> 00:04:24,902
Say it with me!

105
00:04:25,617 --> 00:04:28,207
Coil a long piece of wire around an iron nail.

106
00:04:28,897 --> 00:04:31,137
Connect the ends of the wires to a battery.

107
00:04:31,697 --> 00:04:35,037
Test the iron nail by placing it near some steel clips.

108
00:04:37,514 --> 00:04:38,974
Show me your score hand!

109
00:04:39,254 --> 00:04:40,284
Two fingers?

110
00:04:40,564 --> 00:04:41,934
You beat the Buddies.

111
00:04:42,214 --> 00:04:43,214
High five!

112
00:04:43,792 --> 00:04:45,362
Did you spot the millipede?

113
00:04:45,672 --> 00:04:48,282
It was on the kerb, by the bicycle rack!

114
00:04:48,407 --> 00:04:49,997
Here is a fun fact!

115
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:53,977
A scared millipede coils up tight, like our wire round the nail!

116
00:04:54,217 --> 00:04:57,737
And most millipedes have far fewer than a thousand legs!

117
00:04:57,863 --> 00:04:59,143
Tell someone at home!

118
00:04:59,872 --> 00:05:02,072
Let's read today's key words together!

119
00:05:02,362 --> 00:05:03,122
Ready?

120
00:05:03,409 --> 00:05:04,809
Electrical method.

121
00:05:06,611 --> 00:05:07,911
Electromagnet.

122
00:05:09,705 --> 00:05:10,445
Coil.

123
00:05:11,696 --> 00:05:12,636
Well done!

124
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:15,683
Our crane cannot lift the steel bolt.

125
00:05:15,933 --> 00:05:19,205
And we have no more batteries, so it can never get stronger.

126
00:05:19,225 --> 00:05:21,935
Can the crane get stronger without another battery?

127
00:05:22,205 --> 00:05:23,795
Find out in Part Two!

128
00:05:24,954 --> 00:05:26,055
Say it with us!

129
00:05:26,855 --> 00:05:27,605
Ready?

130
00:05:27,729 --> 00:05:28,389
One!

131
00:05:28,729 --> 00:05:29,429
two!

132
00:05:29,734 --> 00:05:30,909
Now you know!
